      "allowedTypes": ["images"]
    }
  }
}
```

## Using Components in Content Types

Components can be used in content types in two ways:

### 1. Single Component Field

Use a component once in a content type:

```json
{
  "attributes": {
    "defaultSeo": {
      "type": "component",
      "repeatable": false,
      "component": "shared.seo"
    }
  }
}
```

**Example from `global` content type:**
```json
"defaultSeo": {
  "type": "component",
  "repeatable": false,
  "component": "shared.seo"
}
```

### 2. Dynamic Zone Field

Use multiple components in a flexible, dynamic way:

```json
{
  "attributes": {
    "blocks": {
      "type": "dynamiczone",
      "components": ["shared.media", "shared.quote", "shared.rich-text", "shared.slider"]
    }
  }
}
```

**Example from `article` content type:**
```json
"blocks": {
  "type": "dynamiczone",
  "components": ["shared.media", "shared.quote", "shared.rich-text", "shared.slider"]
}
```

## Component Naming Convention

Components are referenced using dot notation: `[category].[component-name]`

**Examples:**
- `shared.media` → `strapi/src/components/shared/media.json`
- `shared.seo` → `strapi/src/components/shared/seo.json`
- `shared.rich-text` → `strapi/src/components/shared/rich-text.json`

## Creating New Components

### Step 1: Create the Component File

Create a new JSON file in the appropriate category folder:

```bash
# Example: Create a new "card" component in the "shared" category
strapi/src/components/shared/card.json
```

### Step 2: Define the Component Structure

```json
{
  "collectionName": "components_shared_cards",
  "info": {
    "displayName": "Card",
    "icon": "layer-group",
    "description": "A reusable card component"
  },
  "options": {},
  "attributes": {
    "title": {
      "type": "string",
      "required": true
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "text"
    },
    "image": {
      "type": "media",
      "multiple": false,
      "allowedTypes": ["images"]
    },
    "link": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  }
}
```

### Step 3: Use the Component in Content Types

```json
{
  "attributes": {
    "featuredCard": {
      "type": "component",
      "repeatable": false,
      "component": "shared.card"
    },
    "contentBlocks": {
      "type": "dynamiczone",
      "components": ["shared.card", "shared.media", "shared.quote"]
    }
  }
}
```

## Component Field Types

Components can use all the same field types as content types:

### Basic Fields
- `string`, `text`, `richtext`
- `email`, `password`
- `number`, `integer`, `float`, `decimal`
- `date`, `time`, `datetime`
- `boolean`
- `enumeration`
- `json`

### Advanced Fields
- `media` - File uploads
- `uid` - Unique identifiers
- `relation` - Relationships to content types
- `component` - Nested components
- `dynamiczone` - Dynamic zones within components

## Best Practices

### 1. Organize by Category
```
strapi/src/components/
├── shared/          # Reusable across multiple content types
├── layout/          # Layout-specific components
├── content/         # Content-specific components
└── forms/           # Form-related components
```

### 2. Naming Conventions
- Use lowercase, hyphenated names: `rich-text`, `hero-banner`
- Use descriptive names: `seo`, `media`, `quote`
- Keep category names short and clear: `shared`, `layout`, `content`

### 3. Component Design
- Keep components focused on a single purpose
- Make components flexible but not overly complex
- Use required fields judiciously
- Add helpful descriptions

### 4. Reusability
- Design components to be reusable across different content types
- Avoid overly specific components that only work in one context
- Consider creating variants rather than highly customized components

## Common Patterns

### 1. Content Block System
```json
// In content types
"content": {
  "type": "dynamiczone",
  "components": [
    "shared.rich-text",
    "shared.media",
    "shared.quote",
    "shared.slider"
  ]
}
```

### 2. SEO Component
```json
// Reusable SEO component
"seo": {
  "type": "component",
  "repeatable": false,
  "component": "shared.seo"
}
```

### 3. Repeatable Components
```json
// Multiple instances of the same component
"testimonials": {
  "type": "component",
  "repeatable": true,
  "component": "shared.testimonial"
}
```

## API Response Structure

When you fetch content with components, the API returns the component data embedded within the content:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "id": 1,
    "title": "My Article",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "__component": "shared.rich-text",
        "body": "<p>This is rich text content</p>"
      },
      {
        "__component": "shared.media",
        "file": {
          "url": "/uploads/image.jpg",
          "alternativeText": "Sample image"
        }
      },
      {
        "__component": "shared.quote",
        "title": "Quote Title",
        "body": "This is a quote body"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```


# Integrating with Frontend